// Hand-curated position availability (positions_race_eras) for cases the
// source data cannot evidence.
//
// tools/import-bbl only asserts availability where it has positive evidence a
// position was played -- a config override, star-player status, or a recorded
// player use in a matching era. That is deliberately strict: the looser "this
// race fielded no teams in this era, so assume the position was available"
// rule it used to apply produced wrong rows (Halfling positions available to
// Human teams). Genuine availability the source data cannot show is restored
// here from the rulebook rosters.
//
// This file lives in after-other-importers, never before, and that is load
// bearing: many of the position references below use the "<raceName>:
// <positionName>" Name external id that NameExternalIdService.forPosition
// builds, and that id is only created by tools/import-bbl's position
// importer. Curating before the importers would create an orphan position
// row under that Name id on a fresh database; when BBL later upserts the
// same real position, supplying both its own numeric external id (already
// resolved to a different, earlier-created row) and that same Name id (now
// resolved to the orphan), the two ids point at different rows and the
// upsert throws PositionUpsertConflictError. Curating after ensures BBL has
// already established that position's identity, so these references resolve
// to the correct existing row instead of racing to create a duplicate.
//
// positions_race_eras is keyed per ERA, not per rules set. "First era" and
// "First Stunty Leeg era" each span CRP, CRP+ and BB2016 together, so one row
// covers all three for those eras.
//
// Each entry re-states the position's existing `name` verbatim, because the
// upsert overlays it -- a mismatched name would rename the position rather
// than leave it alone. `isStarPlayer` is likewise re-stated (false, for every
// entry below -- none of these are star players), since on a fresh database
// this phase creates the row and positions.is_star_player is NOT NULL.
//
// Restoration set: every position with a curated CRP `position_rules_sets`
// entry in data/after-other-importers/position-characteristics.json5 (Tasks
// 3-5) is positive rulebook evidence that position was available to its race
// under First era (which spans CRP, CRP+ and BB2016). The same is true, under
// First Stunty Leeg era (which also spans BB2016, CRP and CRP+), for every
// Stunty-Leeg-handbook-sourced position curated there (Tasks 10-11).
//
// Because this file runs in the after-other-importers phase, its `name`
// re-statements (see below) win over anything a before-other-importers file
// (e.g. races-and-positions.json5) curates for the same position: this phase
// runs later and the upsert overlays whatever name is given here. A future
// rename curated in a before-phase file for a position also listed below
// would therefore be silently reverted by this file on the next import.
// Currently inert -- no position name is curated in both places -- but
// nothing here tests for the overlap, so it is worth knowing about before
// adding one.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],
  positions: [
